## Context

The short paper now targets a causal estimate of JETP acceleration (author decision, 14 September 2026). Establish a credible counterfactual and observable early-stage outcomes before selecting an estimator. More dates or a better matched pool alone do not establish identification. Pre-approval histories and JETP admission may be selectively observed.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First identification challenge: a lender selects projects already near approval
into JETP, while a common calendar shock speeds up every country. A simple
JETP-versus-old-completed-project comparison must fail the causal acceptance
check even if observed country covariates balance. State what additional
assignment or longitudinal evidence could distinguish either bias from an effect.


First documentary acceptance exercise: trace one mature-on-JETP-entry project, one pending proposal and one historical comparator from sources into dated stages. A publication date substituted for an event date, or a pending proposal dropped as missing, must be detected. Record a failed initial extraction before refining the coding protocol.

## Actions

Select 10–15 named JETP investment projects by explicit lender/technology rules, covering different disclosure conditions without claiming representativeness. Define a historical candidate cohort in the same countries/lenders/instruments where feasible. Audit identification→approval, approval→signature and signature→effectiveness/first payment. Track event precision, pre-existing maturity, cancellations, reporting delay and censoring. Coordinate 0721 matching; do not wait for construction or complete four-country reconciliation. Record a feasibility matrix, extraction effort and go/narrow/defer recommendation for each stage.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Selection rules and exclusions documented before outcome comparison
- [ ] Both endpoints and source locators audited for each proposed interval
- [ ] Historical pending/withdrawn proposal coverage and survivorship bias assessed
- [ ] JETP entry and earlier project history distinguished
- [ ] Stage-specific observation decision AND a documented causal-design go/narrow/defer decision for 0730; positive acceleration is never required

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

