## Next executable slice, 14 September 2026

This is the next scientific task for the short paper and is ready to start from
the source registries without waiting for public hosting or manuscript scaffolds.
The observatory date-role fixes improve export safety but do not establish the
missing historical endpoints.

1. Write selection rules before inspecting duration differences. Begin with a
   lender/instrument stratum shared by named JETP and ordinary historical energy
   operations; expand only where the documentary evidence supports it.
2. Execute the first-test triad above: one mature-on-entry JETP project, one pending
   JETP proposal, and one ordinary historical operation. Locate original lifecycle
   documents and record failed/ambiguous extractions. This is a protocol check,
   not the final sample or a speed estimate.
3. Apply the corrected protocol to the agreed 10–15 JETP cases and a defined
   historical candidate frame. Include observable active/withdrawn/cancelled cases;
   the MVP's 97 closed operations are discovery leads, not the sampling frame.
4. Deliver a row-level endpoint/source matrix, a selection-and-exclusion log, and
   a stage-by-stage go/narrow/defer memo for 0730. At minimum record operation and
   project IDs, attribution and entry date, instrument, maturity at entry, both
   endpoints with role/precision/bounds, source locator, observation cutoff,
   censoring/cancellation and extraction effort.

The first useful figure is a coverage diagnostic showing how many cases support
each comparable interval and why others do not. It precedes any acceleration
figure. Prefer approval→signature as a candidate to audit alongside the other
agreed transitions, not a predetermined outcome. If identification histories are
unobservable, explicitly narrow the question rather than substituting pledge age.

## Broader comparator pool and causal-identification audit

User discussion on 14 September opens a pooled/weighted reference from other
beneficiary countries with comparable pre-treatment conditions. Audit this option
alongside within-country comparisons; do not restrict discovery to four countries.
The precise meaning of comparable status remains to be settled in the protocol.
Candidate dimensions include historical income/lending eligibility and energy-sector
conditions, alongside project lender/instrument/technology and maturity. Match
country characteristics at the relevant historical baseline, not today's status;
do not condition on subsequent project success or post-JETP financing choices.

Distinguish two estimands before selecting a design: the effect of project-specific
JETP support, and the total effect of a partnership on a country's eligible energy
pipeline. Audit dated eligibility/admission rules, candidate lists including
rejected/deferred proposals, and any genuine discontinuity or exogenous rollout.
Do not presume such an assignment mechanism exists. For a country-level design,
audit repeated pre- and post-JETP outcomes in both treated and candidate comparator
countries, concurrent reforms, anticipation, spillovers and consistent measurement.
Record donor-pool overlap and exclusions. Four treated countries limit inference;
large project counts are not large numbers of independent policy assignments.

A matched historical pool is not automatically a formal synthetic control.
Old completed operations alone cannot distinguish treatment effects from calendar
changes without further assumptions. Include contemporary non-JETP operations in
the feasibility search where appropriate, and retain unfinished observations.
Deliver a causal-design go/narrow/defer assessment separately from the endpoint
coverage decision. A descriptive benchmark can remain an observatory output if causal
identification is not credible, but it does not complete the causal short-paper path.

Method pointers: World Bank Impact Evaluation in Practice (assignment rules and
counterfactual designs), https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/sief-trust-fund/publication/impact-evaluation-in-practice ;
Abadie, Diamond and Hainmueller, https://www.nber.org/papers/t0335 ; historical
country classifications, https://datahelpdesk.worldbank.org/knowledgebase/articles/906519-world-bank-country-and-lending-groups .

## Author decision: causal short paper, 14 September 2026

Causal identification is the target, not an optional interpretation added after
estimating historical differences. This requirement supersedes earlier language
in this ticket allowing a descriptive benchmark to complete the short-paper path.
The observatory and data paper can proceed independently.

Required design dossier before closing this ticket:

- Define one primary estimand, population, unit and treatment onset: the total
  partnership effect on an eligible pipeline, or a narrower project-support effect.
  Explain which substantive question that choice answers and which it cannot.
  A loan signature cannot define treatment when signature speed is the outcome.
- Compare evidence for candidate designs: a genuine allocation cutoff/exogenous
  rollout if documented; otherwise longitudinal difference-in-differences or a
  synthetic-country comparison with adequate pre-treatment outcomes. Matching
  alone needs an explicit, defensible no-unmeasured-confounding assumption; a
  large donor pool or good balance is not proof of it. Do not invent an instrument.
- Identify the candidate population before observing treatment outcomes. Record
  admission rules, maturity and treatment timing without immortal-time bias;
  separate project selection from policy-wide treatment. Do not match on outcomes
  or variables changed by the JETP when estimating its total effect.
- Audit contemporary untreated comparators and earlier outcomes, common support,
  measurement stability, concurrent policies, anticipation, spillovers and attrition.
  Distinguish missing events from right/interval censoring and cancellation.
- Specify falsification/placebo and sensitivity checks, the level of treatment
  assignment for uncertainty, minimum useful outcome precision and a feasibility
  assessment of statistical power. Four treated countries are not hundreds of
  independent treatments merely because they contain many projects.
- Deliver the evidence audit (including the three-case check and 10–15 JETP cases),
  a short identification memo, and a proposed protocol to freeze before primary
  effect estimation. Record existing outcome inspection; already-read material
  is development evidence, not a prospectively held-out test.

GO means a defensible design with obtainable data. NARROW means a credible causal
claim for a smaller population, intervention or stage, explicitly justified.
DEFER means explain the missing identifying evidence and return an author scope
choice; do not silently substitute a descriptive short paper. Null or adverse
causal effects remain fully acceptable. No completion criterion requires a
statistically significant or positive effect.

Additional exit criteria:

- [ ] Primary estimand/treatment and identification assumptions stated before effect estimation
- [ ] Candidate designs judged against actual assignment/longitudinal evidence
- [ ] Contemporary comparator support, threats, falsification and uncertainty plan documented
- [ ] Frozen-protocol proposal and causal go/narrow/defer memo linked for 0730
